    "hh_split_4": {
      "type": "hh-split",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "layout": "image_left",
        "fallback_image": "hh-photo-holly-portrait.jpg",
        "image_alt": "Holly Baynes",
        "image_position": "object-position: center 25%",
        "logo_mark": "none",
        "heading": "Twenty years in medicine. One hour in a circle in Portugal.",
        "text": "<p>I'm a nurse practitioner. I've spent twenty years in medicine, fifteen of them in heart surgery, and I still love the work.</p><p>At a women's retreat in Portugal, I sat in a circle, drew a guidance card, and started journaling. I didn't expect much. That one hour of sitting together and listening to one another turned into a full circle moment I still think about. Now I hold circles here in Nebraska, with a cup of cacao in everyone's hands.</p>",
        "show_signature": true,
        "signature_mark": "hh-logo-arch-cacao.svg",
        "button_label": "Read my story",
        "button_link": "/pages/our-story"
      }
    },
